    359  f85c							; old filtered value has added to it 1/4 of the differences between
    360  f85c							; the new conversion value and the old filtered value. This causes
    361  f85c							; the filter response to be expoential with a time constant of
    362  f85c							; 4 times the interval between conversions. Since one conversion
    363  f85c							; is performed every 1/20 second and there are five channels, each
    364  f85c							; channel is measured once every 0.25 seconds. This makes the time
    365  f85c							; constant of the filter equal to 0.25 * 4 = 1 second.
